WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:02.934
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:02.934 --> 00:00:03.968
You're here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:07.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.801
Well, guys,
let's get to the news.

00:00:09.801 --> 00:00:11.601
Everyone is talking about
the Supreme Court

00:00:11.601 --> 00:00:13.734
after they made
some pretty major decisions

00:00:13.734 --> 00:00:15.367
over the last few days.

00:00:15.367 --> 00:00:17.367
And let me just
sum it up for you.

00:00:17.367 --> 00:00:19.834
They basically said,
whether it's a gun or a baby,

00:00:19.834 --> 00:00:21.567
you're carrying something.

00:00:21.567 --> 00:00:27.133
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:28.868
That's right.
On Friday, the Supreme Court

00:00:28.868 --> 00:00:31.367
voted to overturn Roe v. Wade.

00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:32.834
I don't have to tell you
that plenty of people

00:00:32.834 --> 00:00:34.467
are furious with
the Supreme Court right now.

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:36.767
And in an attempt
to tamp down the anger,

00:00:36.767 --> 00:00:38.133
the Supreme Court
released this message.

00:00:38.133 --> 00:00:39.501
Watch this.

00:00:39.501 --> 00:00:41.601
-We here at the Supreme Court
recognize that millions

00:00:41.601 --> 00:00:44.167
of Americans are angry
over our recent actions.

00:00:44.167 --> 00:00:46.467
But we really want to hear
what you have to say.

00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:49.801
So, call us at 1-800 --
[ Mumbling ] -- 9,

00:00:49.801 --> 00:00:52.200
or e-mail us at...
[ Speaking quickly ]

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.434
And you can always write to us
at the address on the screen.

00:00:54.434 --> 00:00:56.400
The United States Supreme Court.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.667
Because your opinion matters.

00:00:58.667 --> 00:01:01.367
[ Cheers and applause ]
-You can just write them.

00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:06.033
You can just find the address.

00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:08.334
In response to the ruling,
President Biden said the Court

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:12.000
is literally taking America
back 150 years.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.501
And if there's anyone who knows
what things were like back then,

00:01:14.501 --> 00:01:16.734
it would be President Biden.

00:01:16.734 --> 00:01:22.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:22.367 --> 00:01:24.501
I saw that House Speaker
Nancy Pelosi

00:01:24.501 --> 00:01:28.434
responded to the Court's
decision by reading a poem.

00:01:28.434 --> 00:01:29.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.868 --> 00:01:31.534
Even Democrats were like,
"Look, if this poem

00:01:31.534 --> 00:01:33.167
doesn't start off with
'Clarence Thomas'

00:01:33.167 --> 00:01:34.300
and end with 'Nantucket,'

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:35.334
we don't want to hear
this poem."

00:01:35.334 --> 00:01:37.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.601 --> 00:01:39.701
Meanwhile, after the decision,
Clarence Thomas

00:01:39.701 --> 00:01:42.767
went even further and brought up
banning contraception.

00:01:42.767 --> 00:01:44.968
[ Audience groans ]
It's all part of his plan --

00:01:44.968 --> 00:01:46.834
Operation: Get My Wife
Out of the News."

00:01:46.834 --> 00:01:48.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.734 --> 00:01:50.467
That's right. A new poll
conducted this weekend.

00:01:50.467 --> 00:01:52.501
A majority of Americans said
that they don't agree with

00:01:52.501 --> 00:01:53.667
the Supreme Court's ruling.

00:01:53.667 --> 00:01:55.667
In fact, 59% of Americans said

00:01:55.667 --> 00:01:58.267
that they disapprove
of the ruling.

00:01:58.267 --> 00:02:01.200
And that's not all.
52% of Americans said

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.434
that it's a step backward
for America.

00:02:03.434 --> 00:02:05.901
While 48% said,
"Circle back next week.

00:02:05.901 --> 00:02:07.934
I'm still mad about
the January 6th hearings

00:02:07.934 --> 00:02:10.567
and how everyone just kind of
decided the pandemic was over."

00:02:10.567 --> 00:02:13.100
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:16.400
Is it over?

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:19.334
33% said they don't really
see how politics affect them,

00:02:19.334 --> 00:02:21.400
then paid 100 bucks
to fill their gas tank.

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:22.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.901 --> 00:02:25.200
And finally, 68% said,
"I'm literally too angry

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:27.000
to answer poll questions
right now."

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:31.534
[ Cheers and applause ]
So just hush.

00:02:31.534 --> 00:02:34.300
Switching gears, this weekend,
President Biden left for Germany

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:37.234
to meet with other world leaders
at this year's G7 summit.

00:02:37.234 --> 00:02:39.734
And, as always, the leaders
took a family photo together.

00:02:39.734 --> 00:02:41.400
Here they are.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:42.634
[ Laughter ]
Yeah.

00:02:42.634 --> 00:02:44.801
Looks like "The Bachelorette:
Senior Edition."

00:02:44.801 --> 00:02:46.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.501 --> 00:02:48.000
Did you guys see this?
Over the weekend,

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.467
Rudy Giuliani claimed
that he got slapped

00:02:50.467 --> 00:02:52.968
by a supermarket employee
and even went on to say,

00:02:52.968 --> 00:02:54.934
it felt like
somebody shot him.

00:02:54.934 --> 00:02:56.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.734 --> 00:02:58.434
That sounds pretty scary.
This is real.

00:02:58.434 --> 00:02:59.868
We have
the surveillance footage.

00:02:59.868 --> 00:03:01.868
This is real.
Let's take a look.

00:03:01.868 --> 00:03:03.534
-There's Rudy.

00:03:03.534 --> 00:03:05.334
Oh.
That was it.

00:03:05.334 --> 00:03:09.501
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.501 --> 00:03:11.200
That was it?

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:13.501
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.501 --> 00:03:16.801
He thinks that was a slap?

00:03:16.801 --> 00:03:19.067
Clearly, Rudy didn't see
this year's Oscars.

00:03:19.067 --> 00:03:25.968
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:03:25.968 --> 00:03:27.334
It makes sense
that he freaked out.

00:03:27.334 --> 00:03:29.567
It's been 20 years since Rudy
got a pat on the back.

00:03:29.567 --> 00:03:32.901
You know what I'm saying?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.901 --> 00:03:34.567
Some entertainment news.
This weekend,

00:03:34.567 --> 00:03:36.767
the new movie, "Elvis,"
narrowly edged out

00:03:36.767 --> 00:03:40.767
"Top Gun: Maverick"
for number 1 at the box office.

00:03:40.767 --> 00:03:42.234
And apparently, it's so popular

00:03:42.234 --> 00:03:43.968
that it already inspired
this new promo.

00:03:43.968 --> 00:03:45.200
Watch this.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:47.534
-Elvis" is officially
the number-one movie

00:03:47.534 --> 00:03:48.767
at the box office.

00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:52.167
And if you loved being
transported back to 1955,

00:03:52.167 --> 00:03:55.334
then you'll love
"The Supreme Court."

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:57.000
Now playing in 29 states.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:03.133
-Interesting promo
for the movie.

00:04:03.133 --> 00:04:04.601
Hey, guys, I saw
a new survey that said

00:04:04.601 --> 00:04:06.234
the perfect temperature
for air-conditioning

00:04:06.234 --> 00:04:09.200
during the summer is 64 degrees.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:12.133
That seems cold.
64 degrees is perfect

00:04:12.133 --> 00:04:14.467
if you're training Rocky
inside a meat locker.

00:04:14.467 --> 00:04:15.901
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.901 --> 00:04:17.267
I think it's a perfect
temperature if you want to see

00:04:17.267 --> 00:04:18.901
your dad's nipples
poking through his T-shirt.

00:04:18.901 --> 00:04:21.934
-Oy!
[ Laughter and groans ]

00:04:21.934 --> 00:04:23.400
Oh!
Ay!

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:25.534
-Hey, guys, I heard about
a family in Idaho

00:04:25.534 --> 00:04:27.200
who came home
to a roofless house

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:30.167
after a roofing company
got the wrong address.

00:04:30.167 --> 00:04:34.334
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.334 --> 00:04:35.834
The company was like,
"Uh, good news --

00:04:35.834 --> 00:04:38.434
you got more outdoor space."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.434 --> 00:04:39.868
I like how the neighbor
watched and was like,

00:04:39.868 --> 00:04:40.934
"What a coincidence.

00:04:40.934 --> 00:04:42.000
We're both having
our roofs replaced."

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:46.234
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.234 --> 00:04:48.501
And this went viral.
A news station in Los Angeles

00:04:48.501 --> 00:04:49.901
wanted to have some fun
and surprise

00:04:49.901 --> 00:04:51.767
one of their reporters
for her birthday,

00:04:51.767 --> 00:04:53.300
but things didn't go as planned.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:54.501
Here, take a look at this.

00:04:54.501 --> 00:04:56.901
-Happy birthday!

00:04:56.901 --> 00:04:59.968
Happy birthday to you!
[ Laughter ]

00:04:59.968 --> 00:05:02.033
It's a floating cake.
-Wait. What --

00:05:02.033 --> 00:05:03.234
-Ooh!

00:05:03.234 --> 00:05:05.000
You have to zip up your face,
though.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:07.334
Zip her up really quick.
We gotta see this.

00:05:07.334 --> 00:05:09.534
Watch your hair.
There we go.

00:05:09.534 --> 00:05:10.801
There we -- there --

00:05:10.801 --> 00:05:12.634
Oh!
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.634 --> 00:05:14.801
[ Sad tuba ]
[ Rim shot ]

00:05:14.801 --> 00:05:16.501
-Hey!

00:05:16.501 --> 00:05:23.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:23.601 --> 00:05:24.834
-Yep, they broke the zipper

00:05:24.834 --> 00:05:26.968
and every ratings record
they ever had.

00:05:26.968 --> 00:05:28.701
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.701 --> 00:05:30.534
Viewers were like, "Hey,
if that's the 8:00 a.m. news,

00:05:30.534 --> 00:05:32.000
we can't wait
for the 11:00 p.m. news.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:33.133
Oh, my goodness."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.133 --> 00:05:34.601
That's right,
it's the first time anyone

00:05:34.601 --> 00:05:36.734
has ever seen
a literal news flash.

00:05:36.734 --> 00:05:38.968
There you have it, everybody.
[ Laughter and applause ]

